Knowing pattern category help me understand problem faster. When problem is about creating objects, I think about creational patterns. When problem is about communication, behavioral patterns are more useful. Chapter 6 explain that categories organize patterns by problem type.

Gamma et al. (1995) say design patterns describe common design solution. Categories make this easier to use in real project. Without categories, it is hard to choose correct pattern.

One example is notification system. If I use structural pattern instead of Observer, components become tightly connected. Observer allow many listeners without changing sender code. This make system more flexible.

Another example is chat system. Mediator is better than direct calls because objects do not depend on each other. Behavioral patterns help manage interaction logic.

This lab change how I see patterns. They are not just code, but tools for thinking. Choosing correct category help avoid bad design and make code easier to maintain.

Reference: Gamma et al. (1995), cited in Osmani (2023), Chapter 6.
